OkulAIr — A new lens on your documents.

OkulAIr is an independent fork of Okular, developed by the KDE community.
Upstream project: https://okular.kde.org/
Upstream source: https://invent.kde.org/graphics/okular
Fork source: https://github.com/gkouros/okulair

This fork is not an official KDE project or an official Okular release.
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by KDE or the upstream Okular maintainers.
Upstream names identify the origin of the software.

The inherited software remains the work of its respective copyright holders.
Their file-level notices and upstream author/credit lists remain in place,
including aboutdata.h and source headers. No claim is made to sole authorship
of the inherited code or ownership of upstream names or artwork.

Fork modifications documented on 2026-11-17:
- Introduced the OkulAIr name and tagline in the fork README.
- Added original vector branding and PNG exports under docs/branding/.
- Refined the branding to a document-and-lens mark; fork attribution remains
  in documentation and notices rather than on the active logo.
- Added an AI-assistance architecture and implementation plan.
- Added fork attribution and licensing/distribution guidance.
- Preserved the original README as README.upstream.md and added COPYING as
  an unchanged copy of LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt.

Initial experimental implementation on 2026-11-17:
- Added native desktop chat, summary, and reviewed-highlight workflows.
- Added OpenAI, Anthropic, and compatible streaming adapters.
- Added versioned AI history in a standard PDF note, local recovery, and tests.
- Added native ChatGPT browser authentication and plan model discovery.
- Added API-key presets and model discovery for DeepSeek, Gemini, Groq,
  Mistral, OpenRouter, and Grok, with visible connection errors.
- Added OpenSSL 3 Crypto as an AI-build dependency for identity verification.
- Separated AI connection settings from movable chat docks, added keyboard
  submission and selection/current-view context (with in-memory image inputs).
- Kept highlight generation out of chat, added model author/date metadata,
  and removed assistant Save PDF/Export buttons in favor of normal saving.
- Preserved reading position during background chat-note writes with optional
  annotation navigation, including history undo/redo; manual edits still navigate.
- Added per-PDF/service sharing confirmation with remembered local approval,
  message cards and user-controlled streaming scroll; moved scope/status controls
  around the prompt composer.
- Added persistent image/text/PDF-text chat attachments, rounded message cards,
  batched incremental streaming, clear controls, and icon-and-text scope buttons.
- Added persistent chat tabs and selected figure/text context,
  selection quick actions, and exact-quote evidence navigation.
- Added background, density-aware reading highlights, editable category colors,
  category regeneration, optional manual-highlight explanations, and view filters.
- Added a cancellable request queue and official-client account adapters for
  Gemini, GitHub Copilot and Qwen; fixed saving after grouped annotation removal.
Application, package, and installation identifiers still use upstream names.

